.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt TPOSD-SETUP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tposd-setup
.Nd configure the system for tposd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Installing
.Xr tposd 1
does not change the system configuration;
.Nm
does.
Run it once as root after installing, and again after an upgrade that says
so.
It:
.Bl -bullet
.It
loads the kernel modules
.Xr acpi_ibm 4
and
.Xr acpi_call 8 ,
now and at boot
.Pq Pa /boot/loader.conf ;
.It
gives the PAM service of
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/pam.d/polkit-1 ,
a session stack without
.Xr pam_lastlog 8 ,
whose
.Dq Last login
message makes pkexec abort; the original is kept as
.Pa polkit-1.orig ;
.It
restarts
.Xr devd 8 ,
so it reads the rule for the microphone mute key.
PulseAudio, whose module-devd-detect is connected to devd, exits when devd
restarts; log out and in again afterwards;
.It
sets the OSS
.Dq pcm
level of the default mixer to 1.00 and saves it for the next boot.
.El
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Only show what would be done.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr tposd 1 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5 ,
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr mixer 8 ,
.Xr tposd-mute-led 8
